{
  "meta": {
    "title": "SemIf: decisions without generation",
    "source": "https://github.com/TheoLeeCJ/SemIf-OpenJev",
    "fps": 30,
    "size": [
      1920,
      1080
    ],
    "voice": {
      "backend": "say",
      "voice": "Samantha",
      "rate_wpm": 175
    },
    "glossary": [
      {
        "term": "token",
        "plain": "word"
      },
      {
        "term": "logits",
        "plain": "scores"
      },
      {
        "term": "softmax",
        "plain": "probabilities"
      },
      {
        "term": "KV cache",
        "plain": "notes"
      },
      {
        "term": "prefilled",
        "plain": "reads it once"
      }
    ]
  },
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "title",
      "type": "title",
      "duration_s": 3,
      "narration": [
        "SemIf: semantic ifs, from open models."
      ],
      "data": {
        "title": "SemIf",
        "subtitle": "Semantic ifs from open models",
        "kicker": "Why generate text you immediately parse back into an if?"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "problem",
      "type": "problem",
      "duration_s": 6,
      "narration": [
        "Agents make tons of tiny decisions: which queue gets this ticket, should I retry.",
        "The usual way is to ask a model, let it write out an answer, then parse that text back into an if.",
        "SemIf asks: why write anything at all?"
      ],
      "data": {
        "ticket_label": "Ticket #4812",
        "ticket": [
          "Customer can't reset their password.",
          "The reset email never arrived."
        ],
        "question": "Which queue should handle this?",
        "model": "LLM",
        "answer": [
          "This sounds like an account access",
          "problem, so I'd route it to",
          "account_access."
        ],
        "parser": "parse()",
        "code": "if queue == \"account_access\":"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "how",
      "type": "pipeline",
      "duration_s": 7,
      "narration": [
        "Think multiple-choice, not essay.",
        "You give the model the situation, the question, and your options, labelled A, B and C.",
        "Instead of writing an answer, it just picks a letter."
      ],
      "data": {
        "inputs": [
          "State",
          "Question",
          "Options → A, B, C"
        ],
        "model": "Qwen3.5-4B",
        "stages": [
          "A / B / C scores",
          "Probabilities"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "readout",
      "type": "readout",
      "duration_s": 10,
      "narration": [
        "Here's how.",
        "Before a model writes a single word, it has already scored every possible next word.",
        "Those scores are its answer.",
        "SemIf reads only the scores for A, B and C, and turns them into probabilities.",
        "Account scores high, but it isn't an option, so it's ignored."
      ],
      "data": {
        "question": "Which queue should handle this request?",
        "note": "last position only · no token sampled",
        "vocab": [
          {
            "tok": "The",
            "logit": 18.6
          },
          {
            "tok": "A",
            "logit": 25.0,
            "slot": true
          },
          {
            "tok": "I",
            "logit": 20.3
          },
          {
            "tok": "B",
            "logit": 21.9,
            "slot": true
          },
          {
            "tok": "Account",
            "logit": 22.4
          },
          {
            "tok": "C",
            "logit": 21.2,
            "slot": true
          },
          {
            "tok": "{",
            "logit": 17.8
          }
        ],
        "slots": [
          {
            "letter": "A",
            "option": "account_access",
            "p": 0.94
          },
          {
            "letter": "B",
            "option": "billing",
            "p": 0.04
          },
          {
            "letter": "C",
            "option": "sales",
            "p": 0.02
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "race",
      "type": "race",
      "duration_s": 10,
      "narration": [
        "Why is that faster?",
        "Writing happens one word at a time, and every word is another full pass through the model.",
        "This JSON answer is 111 pieces, so 111 passes.",
        "Reading the scores takes one.",
        "Same model, same questions: five times faster."
      ],
      "data": {
        "left": {
          "label": "Generate JSON array",
          "seconds": 5.332,
          "tokens": 111,
          "passes": 111
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Direct typed logits",
          "seconds": 1.023,
          "tokens": 0,
          "decisions": 21,
          "passes": 1
        },
        "speedup": "5.21x",
        "note": "median of 3 runs",
        "time_scale": 1.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "shared",
      "type": "branch",
      "duration_s": 10,
      "narration": [
        "Now ask 21 questions about the same long document.",
        "The slow part is reading the document, so SemIf reads it once and keeps the model's notes on it.",
        "Each question then only costs its own few words, and all 21 run together.",
        "Twenty decisions a second, instead of two."
      ],
      "data": {
        "prefix_label": "Shared state, ~8,000 chars",
        "cache_label": "KV cache",
        "branches": 21,
        "branch_label": "21 questions, one batch",
        "unit": "decisions / s",
        "rates": [
          {
            "label": "Fresh scoring",
            "v": 2.33
          },
          {
            "label": "Serial prefix reuse",
            "v": 10.75
          },
          {
            "label": "Parallel suffixes",
            "v": 20.03
          }
        ],
        "workload": "37 states × 21 questions"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "numbers",
      "type": "metrics",
      "duration_s": 7,
      "narration": [
        "It gets close to the closed service it's modelled on.",
        "Its confidence can be tuned to match how often it's actually right.",
        "And it runs on four backends, down to your browser."
      ],
      "data": {
        "cards": [
          {
            "label": "TypeSafe-subset agreement",
            "value": "0.845",
            "compare": "Jev (closed): 0.883"
          },
          {
            "label": "Calibration error (authored)",
            "value": "0.068 → 0.038",
            "compare": "temperature scaling"
          },
          {
            "label": "Backends, same prompt",
            "value": "4",
            "compare": "Torch · llama.cpp · MLX · WebGPU"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "outro",
      "type": "outro",
      "duration_s": 4,
      "narration": [
        "No waitlist. Try it in your browser."
      ],
      "data": {
        "headline": "Try it in your browser",
        "url": "github.com/TheoLeeCJ/SemIf-OpenJev"
      }
    }
  ]
}
